WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Research tutorial: Understand the market before you spend.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.600
Page 1 of 3: Research. Ask a market question; reports read real public sources.

3
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.124
Research answers a question about your market from real public sources.

4
00:00:08.124 --> 00:00:10.405
Choose a direction: market, competitors, audience, product, advertising, trends or opportunities.

5
00:00:10.405 --> 00:00:18.525
Then ask in plain words. Your own website can be included as a source.

6
00:00:18.525 --> 00:00:21.784
Finished reports appear under Recent research. Here is one about Dutch candle brands.

7
00:00:21.784 --> 00:00:28.175
A report: a summary, then each finding marked by how well its sources support it.

8
00:00:28.175 --> 00:00:32.949
Sources & limitations list every page that was read, so you can check the evidence yourself.

9
00:00:32.949 --> 00:00:35.549
Page 2 of 3: Insights. Everything your research found, in one place.

10
00:00:38.169 --> 00:00:42.352
Insights brings together what all your research found: findings, opportunities and next actions.

11
00:00:42.352 --> 00:00:47.429
Each finding links to its report and sources. “Create ads from this” starts a brief from it.

12
00:00:47.429 --> 00:00:53.650
The Library holds every report; Saved keeps the findings you want to come back to.

13
00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:56.250
Page 3 of 3: Competitor Analysis. How competitors position themselves, from public sources.

14
00:00:58.871 --> 00:01:05.189
Competitor Analysis opens from Research. It shows how competitors position and advertise themselves.

15
00:01:05.189 --> 00:01:09.372
Keep a list of the competitors you watch, then analyse up to three of them at a time.

16
00:01:09.372 --> 00:01:19.485
OrivenAI reads only public websites and sources; it never sees anyone’s private ad data.
